<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    The wildlife a new map is born with (RimWorld: GenStep_Animals). In its own file rather than appended to
    GenSteps.xml per CLAUDE.md: DefLoader.AddDirectory loads every XML file under a Def folder recursively,
    so a step declared here is wired exactly as if it sat in the shared one and cannot conflict with a lane
    editing that file.

    Order 800 puts it last in the pipeline, after Ruins (650) and Roads (700). Both of those clear whatever
    an earlier step left standing on ground they need, and neither should ever have to decide what to do
    about a living animal in the way — so the animals arrive once the map has stopped changing shape. See
    SimWorld.MapGen.GenStep_Animals for the rest of the reasoning, and SimWorld.Pawns.WildAnimalTuning for
    how many animals BiomeDef.animalDensity actually asks for.
  -->

  <GenStepDef>
    <defName>Animals</defName>
    <order>800</order>
    <workerClass>SimWorld.MapGen.GenStep_Animals</workerClass>
  </GenStepDef>

</Defs>
